 Augustus","s":-26,"e":14,"r":"med","k":"person","d":"His census brings Joseph and Mary to Bethlehem.","p":"augustus_366","ref":"Luke 2:1"},{"id":"w96","t":"Pax Romana","s":-26,"e":180,"r":"med","k":"event","d":"Two centuries of Roman peace and roads that carry the gospel."},{"id":"w45","t":"Herod's Temple rebuilding","s":-19,"e":-19,"r":"ne","k":"work","d":"The Temple expansion that Jesus knew, still underway in his day.","ref":"John 2:20"},{"id":"w97","t":"Tiberius","s":14,"e":37,"r":"med","k":"person","d":"Emperor during John the Baptist's and Jesus's ministries.","p":"tiberius_2852","ref":"Luke 3:1"},{"id":"w98","t":"Caligula","s":37,"e":41,"r":"med","k":"person","d":"Orders his statue placed in the Temple, but dies before it is done."},{"id":"w99","t":"Claudius","s":41,"e":54,"r":"med","k":"person","d":"Expels the Jews from Rome, bringing Aquila and Priscilla to Corinth.","p":"claudius_947","ref":"Acts 18:2"},{"id":"w100","t":"Rome invades Britain","s":43,"e":43,"r":"wo","k":"event","d":"Claudius adds Britain to the empire."},{"id":"w101","t":"Gallio, proconsul of Achaia","s":51,"e":51,"r":"med","k":"person","d":"An inscription at Delphi dates his term, anchoring Paul's timeline.","p":"gallio_1275","ref":"Acts 18:12"},{"id":"w102","t":"Nero","s":54,"e":68,"r":"med","k":"person","d":"The Caesar to whom Paul appealed; later persecutes Christians.","ref":"Acts 25:11"},{"id":"w103","t":"Great Fire of Rome","s":64,"e":64,"r":"med","k":"event","d":"Nero blames the Christians and begins the first persecution."},{"id":"w46","t":"Jewish revolt against Rome","s":66,"e":73,"r":"ne","k":"event","d":"Judea rises against Rome; Jerusalem is besieged."},{"id":"w47","t":"Jerusalem and the Temple destroyed","s":70,"e":70,"r":"ne","k":"event","d":"Titus burns the Temple, as Jesus foretold.","ref":"Matthew 24:2"},{"id":"w48","t":"Fall of Masada","s":73,"e":73,"r":"ne","k":"event","d":"The last Jewish stronghold falls to Rome."},{"id":"w104","t":"Vesuvius buries Pompeii","s":79,"e"